<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAMRAND HALF YEAR PROFIT RISES, SHR FALLS.</title>
<headline>SAMRAND HALF YEAR PROFIT RISES, SHR FALLS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     1.4	   vs 6.3</p>
<p>    Retained income	 1.66 profit vs 0.13 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1.90	  vs 0.45</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.15	  vs 0.12</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.31	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Turnover		  7.08	  vs 0.10</p>
<p>Full name: Samrand Development Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Samrand said that, as the largest development in the</p>
<p>Johannesburg-Pretoria light industrial corridor, it was</p>
<p>confident thats its early momentum can be accelerated.</p>
<p>The earings per share figure was calculated with 126.16</p>
<p>million shares in issue compared to 5.17 million in the same</p>
<p>period last year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
